                     <textLang xml:lang="ar">Arabic</textLang>
                     <title ref="LIT0049IHA#s23IHA" type="acephalous"/>
                     <incipit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#2v">-2v</locus>قَالَ أَلَمْ أَقُلْ لَّكَ إِنَّكَ لَنْ تَسْتَطِيْعَ مَعِي صَبْراً</incipit>
                     <explicit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#22v">-22v</locus>مَا يَاْتِيْهم مِّنْ ذِكْرٍ \ م؟<note>The letter mīm is part of the catchword من . The catchword is partly covered by white repair paper.</note>
                     </explicit>
                     <note>18:75-21:2. The text ends abruptly in the middle of verse 21:2 on fol. 22v. A catchword is partly visible on fol. 22v. Ǧuz' marker in yellow, traced in red on fol. 2v. End of ǧuz' 16 marked with a large letter hā' after the verse marker on fol. 22v. Ihmāl mark (sīn). Deletions. On almost all folios, words rewritten or completed on the following line. Red triple dots as verse markers. Rubrication of Sūrat Maryam. Words and expressions enhanced (takbīr and talwīn) on folios 5v, 12v, 13r, 19v.</note>
                     <note/>
                  </msItem>
